<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Arg-e Bam</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bam is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> province in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, famous for the Arg-e Bam, the largest adobe citadel in the world, which grew on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> trade routes. In 1794 the last Zand ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lotf-ali-khan">Lotf Ali Khan</a>, was betrayed and captured there. An earthquake in December 2003 killed some 26,000 people and destroyed much of the citadel, now a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bam-iran.jpg" alt="Bam" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Safa.daneshvar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:010213-Kerman-IMG_0371-2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
